# Read by ~/.config/mx-tui/commands/zoom. Credentials live here, never in
# mx-tui's config.toml and never on a command line.
#
# ── The easy way: your Personal Meeting link ──────────────────────────────────
# Open https://zoom.us/profile, find "Personal Meeting ID", and copy the whole
# invite link underneath it — it already carries the passcode. Paste it here,
# uncomment, and /zoom works with no Zoom app registration at all.
#
# ZOOM_LINK="https://us05web.zoom.us/j/1234567890?pwd=AbCdEf"
#
# ── The other way: a fresh meeting every time ─────────────────────────────────
# https://marketplace.zoom.us → Develop → Build App → **Server-to-Server OAuth**.
# Give it the scope `meeting:write:meeting:admin`, activate it, then copy its three
# values here. Use this if you ever need two calls running at once.
#
# ZOOM_ACCOUNT_ID=""
# ZOOM_CLIENT_ID=""
# ZOOM_CLIENT_SECRET=""
